# Caddy site blocks for nakhatra.com.
#
# Caddy runs on the host (systemd, not in the compose stack) and already
# terminates TLS for other projects on this VPS, so this is appended to
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile rather than shipped as a container. Kept in the repo
# because the only other copy is on the server, where nothing reviews it.
#
# TLS is a Cloudflare Origin Certificate, matching kundali.riocut.com and the
# egfilm.xyz hosts. The records are proxied (orange cloud), so visitors get
# Cloudflare's edge certificate and this one is only ever presented to
# Cloudflare — which is the whole point of an origin cert. It is not publicly
# trusted, so hitting the origin IP directly will warn; that is expected.
#
# Cloudflare's SSL/TLS mode must be **Full (strict)**. On "Flexible" Cloudflare
# speaks plain HTTP to this origin, Caddy redirects it to HTTPS, and the two
# bounce the request between them until the browser gives up.
#
# Apply with:
#     sudo caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile   # never reload unvalidated
#     sudo systemctl reload caddy                         # reload, not restart:
#                                                         # restart drops the other sites

# ==========================================
# Nakhatra Web
# ==========================================
nakhatra.com {
	tls /etc/caddy/certs/cloudflare_nakhatra.crt /etc/caddy/certs/cloudflare_nakhatra.key
	# The Next.js container publishes on loopback only; Caddy is the only
	# way in from outside.
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
}

# One canonical host. Serving the site on both spellings splits analytics,
# splits the Google OAuth origin allowlist, and gives search engines two URLs
# for every page.
www.nakhatra.com {
	tls /etc/caddy/certs/cloudflare_nakhatra.crt /etc/caddy/certs/cloudflare_nakhatra.key
	redir https://nakhatra.com{uri} permanent
}

# ==========================================
# Nakhatra API
# ==========================================
# A separate host rather than a path under the web app: apps/mobile talks to
# FastAPI directly and needs a base URL that is not the Next.js server. The web
# app keeps calling it over the Docker network (FASTAPI_URL), so browser traffic
# does not come through here at all.
api.nakhatra.com {
	tls /etc/caddy/certs/cloudflare_nakhatra.crt /etc/caddy/certs/cloudflare_nakhatra.key
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:28001
}
